Title: F2-M08 — The Winter Ledger (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

FADE IN:

INT. SNOWBOUND BUNKER, STAGING AREA GATE - LATE AFTERNOON

[[AMBIENCE: wind howling at the door, a stove ticking, trucks warming up outside]]
[[MUSIC: cold, grinding tension]]

A road map of the pass is spread across an ammunition crate. COMMANDER SAVA, LENKA and PETROV stand over it. Snow is already on Petrov's shoulders.

PETROV
(alert)
The convoy carries copies of the ledgers. The mountain pass will close when the storm reaches the ridge.

LENKA
(measured)
The enemy knows what is in those trucks. Expect attacks at both ends of the route.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: staging area and headquarters at the west gate, gorge road east, ravine bridge, hairpin in the rocks, saddle, pass exit; storm front drawn at the ridge]]

PETROV
Gate to the exit is twenty-two minutes if nothing stops us. Gorge road, the ravine bridge, the hairpin, the saddle. The hairpin is the bad one; rockets in the rocks fire down on anything slow.

LENKA
Copies are a clue, Commander. The originals in that headquarters are the proof. If we lose the staging area, whatever reaches the far side cannot be checked against anything.

COMMANDER SAVA
(clipped)
So the risk is in both directions. Pull the escort forward and the staging area falls. Leave it behind and the trucks die at the hairpin. We do not have enough for both and the storm does not care.

PETROV
Three trucks. Repair trucks keep the tanks moving; engineers can rebuild a bridge, sixty seconds a span, under fire.

COMMANDER SAVA
(firm)
Get the convoy through before the weather closes the pass. Protect the records even if the rear guard must fall back.

COMMANDER SAVA
(quieter)
And watch the road behind the convoy, not just ahead of it. Whoever is paying for this war knows exactly where we are thin.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

FADE OUT.
